I'm considering the hardware implications. Using a tree structure minimizes the critical path, making the design faster. I'll use 4-bit counters for the 8-bit groups and a 3-bit counter for the 7-bit part, then cascade the adders to sum the counts. This approach balances area and speed efficiently.

